 "text": "Good morning, and thank you for having me. Today I will talk about how we measured heat stress on coral reefs. We used 20 years of satellite temperature records. For each reef we computed degree heating weeks, which is the accumulated heat above the summer maximum. We then trained a model on reef depth and heat stress. The model predicted leaching three weeks in advance. This is two weeks earlier than the current warning system. The errors were not random. They clustered on deep reefs. Thanks. Thank you.",
